Completed the [Markdown referee report](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/scratch/analytic_2/analytic_2_report.md), covering all seven claims with verdicts, corrected statements, proofs, counterexamples, and references.

Main findings:

- C2’s \(1/(j+2)\) upper bound survives for fixed degree.
- Cubic decoding can tolerate \(N^{1/6-\epsilon}\) absolute error using conic recovery.
- The proposed rank formula and universal curvature lower bound have exact counterexamples.
- The uniform-degree \(L[1/2]\) argument has an additional candidate-counting gap.

[Reproducible checks](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/scratch/analytic_2/referee_checks.py) include 3,988 passing ladder cases. Repository files were unchanged.